@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+// Zeppelin F-238 (Loot Beam): a beam of light over every NPC corpse that can still be looted, tinted by the
+// rarest item in its loot. Ported from wxl-loot-beam (manatactical / WarcraftXL, GPL-3.0-or-later):
+// src/LootBeam.cpp, src/BeaconRenderer.cpp, src/UnitFields.hpp, src/LootFields.hpp.
+//
+// The WarcraftXL module drew with a raw IDirect3DDevice9 and found its data through hooks and client
+// offsets. Here the unit walk is ClntObjMgrEnumVisibleObjects, the corpse state is CGUnitData (health,
+// UNIT_DYNAMIC_FLAGS, UNIT_FIELD_PADDING), the loot is CGLootInfo, and the beam is drawn with the engine's
+// own fixed-function Gx draw (vertex colour, no texture, no shader) inside the world pass, so D3D9 and the
+// Vulkan device both draw it and the world depth buffer occludes it. Its settings are lootBeam* CVars.
+//
+// This program is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU
+// General Public License as published by the Free Software Foundation, either version 3 of the License, or
+// (at your option) any later version.
+#ifndef WOW_SOURCE_WORLDCLIENT_LOOTBEAM_LOOTBEAM_H
+#define WOW_SOURCE_WORLDCLIENT_LOOTBEAM_LOOTBEAM_H
+
+namespace Zep::LootBeam {
+    // Registers the lootBeam* CVars. Called once at start-up (WorldParam_CVar.cpp), before FrameXML loads,
+    // so the Video Options page (ZepLootBeamOptions.lua) can see them.
+    void RegisterCVars();
+
+    // Scans the visible units, advances the fades and draws every beacon. Called once per world frame from
+    // CGWorldFrame's render, beside the spell visuals: the world's depth buffer is complete and the world's
+    // view and projection are still bound.
+    void Render();
+}
+
+#endif
